body:
The field picker uses `availableFields = fieldOptions.map(f => f.value)` which includes all object fields, but the runtime UserFilters dropdown/toggle UX only works well for fields with discrete options (plugin-list auto-derives from `select`/`multi-select`/`boolean` or fields with `options`). Since this UI doesn’t let the user configure `type`/`options`, selecting a free-text/date field will typically render a filter badge with an empty popover (non-functional). Consider deriving `availableFields` from `objectDef.fields` and only offering fields with `options` or a supported type, or expand the editor to configure `type/options` for non-option fields.
```suggestion
                                        {(() => {
                                            // Only expose fields that are backed by discrete options or supported types.
                                            const discreteFieldValues = fieldOptions
                                                .filter((fo: any) => {
                                                    const hasOptions = Array.isArray(fo.options) && fo.options.length > 0;
                                                    const type = fo.type as string | undefined;
                                                    const isSupportedType = type === 'select' || type === 'multi-select' || type === 'boolean';
                                                    return hasOptions || isSupportedType;
                                                })
                                                .map((fo: FieldOption | any) => fo.value);

                                            const selectableFields = availableFields.filter(fv => discreteFieldValues.includes(fv));

                                            if (selectableFields.length === 0) {
                                                return (
                                                    <span className="text-xs text-muted-foreground">
                                                        {t('console.objectView.ufNoFields')}
                                                    </span>
                                                );
                                            }

                                            return (
                                                <select
                                                    data-testid="uf-add-field"
                                                    className="text-xs h-6 w-full border rounded px-1"
                                                    value=""
                                                    onChange={(e: React.ChangeEvent<HTMLSelectElement>) => {
                                                        if (!e.target.value) return;
                                                        const newField = { field: e.target.value };
                                                        updateField('userFilters', { ...uf, fields: [...currentFields, newField] });
                                                        e.target.value = '';
                                                    }}
                                                >
                                                    <option value="">{t('console.objectView.ufAddField')}</option>
                                                    {selectableFields
                                                        .filter(fv => !currentFields.some((cf: any) => cf.field === fv))
                                                        .map(fv => {
                                                            const fo = fieldOptions.find(o => o.value === fv);
                                                            return (
                                                                <option key={fv} value={fv}>
                                                                    {fo?.label || fv}
                                                                </option>
                                                            );
                                                        })}
                                                </select>
                                            );
                                        })()}
```
